    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0681" n="669" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg669"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.9411/129: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Matthews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>(<hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>) <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-23T13:00:00+02:00">October 23, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>804. Chauvel<anchor n="89" xml:id="d713-f1"/> showed me this morning a telegram
                    received from Arsene-Henry<anchor n="90" xml:id="d713-f2"/> at Tokyo under date
                    of October 22. That telegram reported that while there seemed to be no secret
                    clause to the recent tripartite pact he had ascertained that there was a <hi
                        rendition="#italic">procès-verbal</hi> specifically providing that Japan
                    would not be required automatically to make war on the United States if we
                    become involved in hostilities against Germany as a result of action taken by
                    the latter. This <hi rendition="#italic">procès-verbal</hi>, said Henry,
                    specifically provided that Japan should have the right to examine the
                    circumstances before taking any position.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d713-f1" n="89" xml:id="d713-f1-content">
                <p>Jean Chauvel, head of Far Eastern section, French Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d713-f2" n="90" xml:id="d713-f2-content">
                <p>Charles Arsène-Henry, French Ambassador in Japan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
